        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Semiconductor economics is dominated by yield — the fraction of good dies per wafer.\nA leading-edge fab costing $20B produces wafers at $20,000 each. Die yield converts\nthat wafer cost into cost per die. Learning curves drive yield up over time, making\nnewer nodes economical as the fab \"learns.\""
    },
